  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Sustainable Entrepreneurship-Led Poultry Transformation Program (SEPTP)  - ILRI</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Program Overall Goal:&#xa0;Contribute to&#xa0;facilitating a transformative program that enables enterprises in the poultry value chain to thrive and unlock work opportunities that guarantee reliable income for 100,000 young women and men of ages 18-35 years&#xa0;across 12&#xa0;states in Nigeria&#xa0;states.
Program Objectives:
&#xd8;&#xa0;&#xa0;To promote dignified work for women and youth through engagement in poultry.
&#xd8;&#xa0;&#xa0;To increase individual and household income for women and young people in poultry by creating access to domestic and international markets and boosting financial inclusion.
&#xd8;&#xa0;&#xa0;To develop women&apos;s and young people&#x2019;s capacity to build viable and sustainable agribusinesses through information, innovation, and entrepreneurial training.
&#xd8;&#xa0;&#xa0;To address the constraints in the poultry sector and increase women and youth participation in commercially viable poultry agribusinesses across target states.
&#xa0;
Program Theory of Change:
The SEPTP Program envisions&#xa0;that: If&#xa0;we enhance the entrepreneurial and technical capacity of organized, women-owned new and existing poultry enterprises, and&#xa0;enable them access to affordable inputs and services through appropriate linkages, they will produce competitively, access markets, obtain reliable income, sustain dignified and fulfilling work in poultry business.</narrative>
  </description>
